 will create a new iterator that places a copy"},{"DocComment":" of `separator` between `Some(_)` items, particularly just right before the subsequent"},{"DocComment":" `Some(_)` item."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For example, consider the following non-fused iterator:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" Some(1) -> Some(2) -> None -> Some(3) -> Some(4) -> ..."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If this non-fused iterator were to be interspersed with `0`,"},{"DocComment":" then the interspersed iterator will produce:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" Some(1) -> Some(0) -> Some(2) -> None -> Some(0) -> Some(3) -> Some(0) ->"},{"DocComment":" Some(4) -> ..."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In case `separator` does not implement [`Clone`] or needs to be"},{"DocComment":" computed every time, use [`intersperse_with`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut a = [0, 1, 2].into_iter().intersperse(100);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(0));   // The first element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(1));   // The next element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(2));   // The last element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), None);       // The iterator is finished."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `intersperse` can be very useful to join an iterator's items using a common element:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let words = [\"Hello\", \"World\", \"!\"];"},{"DocComment":" let hello: String = wo